Description: CVE-2026-55973 - fix stack buffer overflow in find_closest_of_type()
 A malformed qname containing a zero-length (root) label part-way through the
 name causes find_closest_of_type() to loop past the end of the name buffer.
 With a zero label length, the pointer/length advance (qname += lablen + 1;
 qnamelen -= lablen + 1;) only steps by one byte and the size_t qnamelen never
 reaches zero as intended, allowing an out-of-bounds walk that can lead to a
 stack buffer overflow. This adds a guard that stops the label-stripping loop
 when a zero-length label is encountered.
 .
 Only the services/cache/dns.c hunk of upstream commit 96f8755 is applied here.
 The services/mesh.c dns-error-reporting (RFC9567) hunk is intentionally omitted
 because that feature does not exist in unbound 1.13.1 (the version shipped in
 Debian bullseye), so the corresponding code path is not present and the
 reporting trigger vector is unreachable on this release.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/96f875552023c0ccf376ebe050519f12f3371dc9
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-08-18
---
--- a/services/cache/dns.c
+++ b/services/cache/dns.c
@@ -217,6 +217,8 @@ find_closest_of_type(struct module_env* env, uint8_t* qname, size_t qnamelen,

 		/* snip off front label */
 		lablen = *qname;
+		if(lablen == 0)
+			break;
 		qname += lablen + 1;
 		qnamelen -= lablen + 1;
 	}
Description: CVE-2026-44690 - Fix cross-zone wildcard cache poisoning via RRSIG.labels manipulation
 An attacker could poison the aggressive NSEC cache with wildcard-expanded
 records whose RRSIG signer is outside the authoritative zone, by manipulating
 the RRSIG labels field. This allowed cross-zone cache poisoning (CWE-345).
 .
 The fix hardens three places:
 .
  * validator/val_sigcrypt.c: reject an RRSIG whose labels count is lower than
    the label count of the signer name (an impossible-to-be-valid wildcard).
  * validator/validator.c: postpone the aggressive-NSEC wildcard cache update
    until the positive wildcard proof has actually succeeded, instead of
    caching the expansion eagerly.
  * services/cache/rrset.c: before caching a wildcard expansion, verify that
    the wildcard canonical parent falls within the authority of every RRSIG
    signer of the rrset (dname_subdomain_rrsig_signers), otherwise drop it.
 .
 The internal helper rrsig_get_signer() is exported from validator/val_utils.c
 for reuse by the rrset cache. A regression test (testdata/rrsig_agr_wild.rpl)
 from the upstream fix is included; testbound auto-discovers testdata/*.rpl.
 .
 This is a backport of the upstream fix to 1.13.x: the target predates the
 EDE/reason_bogus parameter of dnskey_verify_rrset_sig(), so the *reason_bogus
 assignments from the upstream hunk are omitted while the security check is
 preserved.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/f7637a4f1811f4a9331707d8a95cf0af65a97c0f
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/3d5e6c06923eff9eac2f5e31a69c43a15ca9d3c2
