Description: CVE-2026-42959 - Fix crash during DNSSEC validation of malicious content.
 val_fill_reply() in validator/val_utils.c computed the write offsets for the
 ADDITIONAL section using orig->ns_numrrsets instead of chase->ns_numrrsets.
 Because chase is the reply being (re)built and its ns_numrrsets can differ
 from the original reply, this could index chase->rrsets[] beyond the slots
 that have actually been initialized, dereferencing an uninitialized rrset
 pointer and crashing the validator when processing malicious content.
 The fix uses chase->ns_numrrsets for both ADDITIONAL-section write offsets,
 matching the counters used to fill the answer and authority sections.
